<h2>🎨 Step 7: Flutter UI Tree View Integration Workflow</h2>

<p>To implement an interactive 5-level expandable tree view in Flutter (using widgets like <code>ExpansionTile</code> or <code>ListView</code>):</p>

<ol>
  <li><strong>Render Levels 1–3:</strong> Bind the <code>dasha</code> array from <code>/full-report</code> to nested <code>ExpansionTile</code> widgets (Maha &rarr; Antar &rarr; Pratyantar).</li>
  <li><strong>Attach Expansion Callbacks:</strong> Pass an <code>onExpansionChanged</code> callback to the Pratyantar-level <code>ExpansionTile</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Dynamic On-Demand Fetching:</strong> When expanded, if the sub-tree state is empty, display a <code>CircularProgressIndicator</code> and call <code>JyothisyaApiService.fetchPranaDashaTree()</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Update State:</strong> Call <code>setState()</code> or update your state management store (Provider, Bloc, Riverpod) to render the nested <code>sookshma_dashas</code> and <code>prana_dashas</code>.</li>
</ol>

